msgid "Tools"
msgstr "Espleches"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid "Isotope Table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:453
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenuitem>Isotope Table...</guimenuitem> shows you the isotopes of "
"the elements."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:456
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are different kinds of isotopes, some are stable, some are not. The "
"unstable isotopes can decay as alpha-rays are two different beta-rays. These "
"differences are encoded by using different colors."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <quote>Isotope Table</quote> window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:467
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kalzium; can display the isotopes of a range of elements"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:474
#, no-c-format
msgid "Risk/Security Phrases"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:475
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The R/S Phrases, also known as Risk and Safety Statements, R/S statements, R/"
"S numbers, and R/S sentences, is a system of hazard codes and phrases for "
"labeling dangerous chemicals and compounds. The R/S phrase of a compound "
"consists of a risk part (R) and a safety part (S), each followed by a "
"combination of numbers. Each number corresponds to a phrase. The phrase "
"corresponding to the letter/number combination has the same meaning in "
"different languages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid "Glossary"
msgstr "Glossari"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:484
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Glossary gives you definitions of the most used tools in chemistry as "
"well as some knowledge data. On the left side of the windows you can see the "
"tree of items. On top, there are chemical terms, below that there is a "
"second tree of laboratory-tools."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:485
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the top of the widget you can see a searchbar. If you type in the bar the "
"trees will be adjusted immediately. The small button in the right end of the "
"searchbar will clear it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:493
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <quote>Glossary</quote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid "Plot Data"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenuitem>Plot Data...</guimenuitem> dialog allows you to plot some "
"information about elements. The X-axis represents a range of elements (from "
"one number to a higher number). You set this range using the <guilabel>First "
"Element</guilabel> and <guilabel>Last Element</guilabel> fields on the "
"dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:509
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <quote>Plot Data</quote> Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kalzium; can plot some data about a range of elements."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:517
#, no-c-format
msgid "Equation Solver"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:518
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenuitem>Equation Solver</guimenuitem> enables the user to solve "
"chemical equations. This is an example:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:521
#, no-c-format
msgid "aH2O + bCO2 -> cH2CO3"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:522
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The computed equation will be displayed on the right side of the window. As "
"you can see in the first example you can also define the value of one or "
"more coefficients. The other coefficients will be adjusted. Furthermore, it "
"is possible to use brackets around elements or electronic charges as shown "
"in the last two examples."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:530
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <quote>Equation Solver</quote> Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:532
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kalzium; can solve chemical equations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:539
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sidebar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:548
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Overview</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Overview</guilabel> tab is the first one and it shows you an "
"overview of the element the mouse is over."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:556
#, no-c-format
msgid "State of Matter"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:558
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>State of Matter</guilabel> tab is the second in the navigation "
"panel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:559 index.docbook:614
#, no-c-format
msgid "You are first presented with the following icons and text:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:566
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <quote>State of Matter</quote> Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:568
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kalzium; can show you which elements are solid/liquid/vaporous at a given "
"temperature."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:575
#, no-c-format
msgid "Timeline"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:577
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Timeline</guilabel> feature allows you to explore the elements "
"of the set time period. This is great for getting a feel for how the PSE "
"evolved over time, as more and more elements were discovered. If you move "
"the slider you will notice that some elements disappear if you move it to "
"the left and reappear if you move it to the right. Furthermore the number "
"will change constantly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:584
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The number represents the date you are looking at. If you move the slider to "
"&eg; 1856 you will only see the elements which where known in the year 1856."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:590
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will notice that some elements are not even shown in the current year. "
"This is because some of the elements have not been discovered yet but are "
"predicted to exist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:602
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <quote>Timeline</quote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:604
#, no-c-format
msgid "The PSE back in time (elements known in 1856)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:611
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Calculate</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Calculate</guilabel> tab is the last in the sidebar. It allows "
"you to calculate molecules weights."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:621
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Calculate</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:623
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Calculate</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:629
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show Legend"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:630
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenuitem>Show Legend</guimenuitem> action allows you to display the "
"legend for the scheme you are in (Groups, Family, Blocks). The legend is "
"displayed by default but if you hide it, it will stay hidden until you "
"choose to show it. &kalzium; will keep this setting in its configuration "
"file, so that the next time you run it, the setting will be as you left it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:639
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &kalzium;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:641
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kalzium; has many configuration options, which you can access by opening "
"the configuration dialog by selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure &kalzium;...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> "
"from the menu."
msgstr ""

